Subject: [PATCH 363/638] [AROS] Drive Mojo Channel from a reader task

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: channel-aros-core-compile-pass
ROOT_CAUSE: Mojo core still selected ChannelPosix on AROS, binding browser IPC to unavailable socket watcher and fd-passing semantics.
FIX_REASON: Select ChannelAros, receive Exec packets on a dedicated scheduled reader task, marshal packets onto the Mojo IO runner, and serialize platform handles through the proven AROS substrate.
SCOPE: mojo/core/BUILD.gn; mojo/core/channel_aros.{cc,h}
VALIDATION: mojo/core:impl_for_embedder compiles at -j32 with channel_aros.o; the underlying packet/handle transport passes focused hosted validation.
RISK: ChannelAros has not yet passed an end-to-end Mojo invitation; upgrade offers are rejected and POSIX writev tuning is intentionally inert.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: compiled POSIX dependency rejected -> dedicated AROS reader task -> IO-runner dispatch -> Channel managed read buffer -> clean core object/stamp build.
Evidence:-channel-aros-20260728
